From c44f73d101afd526e0467cfd06026334a9565d06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:42:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] ACPI: SBS: Do not report discharging while on AC
To: "Rafael J. Wysocki" <rafael@kernel.org>,
    linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org
Cc: Len Brown <lenb@kernel.org>,
    Sebastian Reichel <sre@kernel.org>,
    linux-pm@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

While a charge limit holds the battery on AC, the gauge reports small
discharge currents of a few tens of mA from time to time. The driver
then switches to discharging, and user space shows a remaining time of
several days although the system runs on AC.

The ACPI battery driver handles the same situation by checking whether
the system is supplied. Do the same and report not charging, or full
when the battery says so, while the system is supplied.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/acpi/sbs.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/sbs.c b/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
index 0935fd776..772903fe9 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
@@ -169,7 +169,7 @@ static int acpi_sbs_battery_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 	acpi_battery_get_state(battery);
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
-		if (battery->rate_now < 0)
+		if (battery->rate_now < 0 && power_supply_is_system_supplied() <= 0)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 		else if (battery->rate_now > 0)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
